spes PON restart reason (0185): read and log only; the one-register write allow-list, unused yet.

Before any PMIC write for "reboot to fastboot" (ios-flame writes PON SOFT_RB_SPARE; Xiaomi's ABL ignored
the IMEM cookie alone, run 2026-11-17: Mi-logo boot loop), this run only reads. sweet_spmi_read's
allow-list gains the four PM6125 PON registers SID 0 0x801 (revision), 0x804 (type), 0x805 (subtype)
and 0x88F (SOFT_RB_SPARE); with sweetusb=2 the USB start logs them and the value the write would use.
bsd/dev/spes_spmi_allow.h holds the future write's checks, free of kernel headers so
tests/test_spes_spmi_allow.py compiles it from this patch: spes_spmi_write_allowed() is true only for
SID 0, 0x88F, length 1 (the user's allow-list); spes_pon_bootloader_value() keeps bit 0 and sets
bits 7:1 to 2 (Linux qpnp_pon_set_restart_reason, PON gen2) and refuses any subtype other than 4/5.
Sources: live FDT qcom,pm6125@0 qcom,power-on@800 (store-hard-reset-reason); Xiaomi qpnp-power-on.c
(SOFT_RB_SPARE = base + 0x8F, GENMASK(7,1), reason << 1), qpnp-power-on.h (BOOTLOADER = 0x02).

diff --git a/bsd/dev/spes_spmi_allow.h b/bsd/dev/spes_spmi_allow.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dc08042
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bsd/dev/spes_spmi_allow.h
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+/*
+ * PMIC (SPMI) write allow-list for spes, kept free of kernel headers so tests/test_spes_spmi_allow.py
+ * compiles this very file on the host (0185).
+ *
+ * The user allowed exactly ONE register: PM6125 (SID 0) PON SOFT_RB_SPARE, 0x88F, one byte, for the
+ * "reboot to fastboot" reason. Live FDT: qcom,pm6125@0 (reg <0 0>) qcom,power-on@800 (reg 0x800 0x100,
+ * qcom,store-hard-reset-reason). Linux (Xiaomi qpnp-power-on.c): SOFT_RB_SPARE = base + 0x8F;
+ * PON_RESTART_REASON_BOOTLOADER = 0x02; PON gen2 (PERPH_SUBTYPE 0x805 = 4 or 5) writes GENMASK(7,1)
+ * with reason << 1. Everything else is refused.
+ */
+#ifndef SPES_SPMI_ALLOW_H
+#define SPES_SPMI_ALLOW_H
+
+#define SPES_PON_SID            0u
+#define SPES_PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE  0x88Fu
+#define SPES_PON_SUBTYPE        0x805u
+
+/* true only for SID 0, address 0x88F, exactly one byte. */
+static inline bool
+spes_spmi_write_allowed(uint32_t sid, uint32_t addr, uint32_t len)
+{
+	return sid == SPES_PON_SID && addr == SPES_PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE && len == 1;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The SOFT_RB_SPARE value for "bootloader" from the register's current value, as Linux's masked
+ * write: keep bit 0, bits 7:1 = 2. Only for PON gen2 (subtype 4 or 5); -1 = do not write.
+ */
+static inline int
+spes_pon_bootloader_value(uint8_t old, uint8_t subtype)
+{
+	if (subtype != 0x04 && subtype != 0x05) {
+		return -1;
+	}
+	return (int)((old & 0x01u) | (0x02u << 1));
+}
+
+#endif /* SPES_SPMI_ALLOW_H */
